# CDASE Session Gate

This machine supports **CDASE** (Context-Driven AI Software Engineering).
Each new conversation MUST start with an explicit opt-in — CDASE is never assumed.

## First turn (before any other work)

If the user has **not** yet declared CDASE on/off this session, ask:

> **Apply CDASE in this session?** (yes / no)

Then **stop and wait** for the answer. Do not read files, run tools, or start tasks until they reply.

## No `cdase/` folder in the repo → confirmation is MANDATORY

Before starting the very first task, note whether the project repo has a `cdase/`
folder at its root.

- If there is **no `cdase/` folder**, CDASE is not initialized here. Then, **whatever
  the user's first message is** (even a direct task request like "I'm joining the
  project" or "add feature X"), do **not** silently begin the work: state that there
  is no `cdase/` folder in the repo, ask **"Apply CDASE in this session? (yes / no)"**,
  and **stop for the answer**. This guarantees the following job is CDASE-based (or
  explicitly not).
- On **yes**: initialize CDASE — create `<repo>/cdase/` at the repo root and **commit
  it** — before doing the requested task.
- On **no**: proceed as a normal assistant; do not create `cdase/`.

If a `cdase/` folder already exists, a plain yes/no is enough.

## Interpreting the answer

| User says | Session mode |
|---|---|
| yes, y, cdase, cdase on, apply cdase | **CDASE ON** — load the `cdase` skill (`~/.cursor/skills/cdase/SKILL.md`), run charter boot |
| no, n, skip, cdase off, normal mode | **CDASE OFF** — normal assistant; ignore the CDASE skill |

If the first message already contains a clear choice (`cdase yes`, `no cdase`, etc.), honor it without re-asking — **unless** there is no `cdase/` folder, in which case still confirm before starting work.

## While the session runs

- **CDASE ON**: Read `~/.cursor/skills/cdase/SKILL.md`, then follow `charter.md` boot (`check` → lazy `login`/`inbox`).
- **CDASE OFF**: Do not load the CDASE skill unless the user says `cdase on`.
- Mid-session toggle: `cdase on` / `cdase off` switches mode immediately.

## Input is host-native (never a browser)

When CDASE needs input (the opt-in, or the one-time user profile), present it with your
host's richest native input UI — in Cursor, the multiple-choice / question card — and fall
back to plain text if the host has none. CDASE never opens a browser or serves its own UI.

## CDASE OFF means

- No charter boot, no stage gates, no HARD STOPs, no templates enforcement.
- The Hub is inactive unless the user re-enables CDASE.
